\newlabel{tab:model_comparison}{{3}{20}{Performance comparison of model architectures on the full 16-feature set, sorted by test AUPRC. LSTM models trained with 3 random seeds; tuned LR, XGBoost, and untuned logistic regression with a single run each. Persistence baseline uses $\hat {y}(t+1) = y(t)$. Random baseline equals test set prevalence (45.9\%). Gap = Train $-$ Test AUPRC, so a negative value means the model scores higher on the test period than on the training period}{table.3}{}}
